{
  "file": "crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs",
  "item": "mod[tests]/impl[Project/Domain]/fn[node_path]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "Source-tool tests publish OutlineId addresses and retain mapped NodeIds\n directly in dependencies. This required Domain method is unused in\n those flows; stable-path and filesystem-storage tests use other domains."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs` `mod[tests]/impl[Project/Domain]/fn[node_path]` is a function-level coverage exception. It sits in fenced commentary and gives a substantive reason, and the reason matches the source.\n\n- **Where it is called.** The only non-test caller of `node_path` in the crate is `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs#fn[edge_fingerprint]`, which calls it for edge targets.\n- **Why the `Project` fixture never reaches it.** In `Project`'s `Domain` impl, `outgoing_edges` always returns an empty list. `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` ignore the node and do not call `node_path`. `source_node` and `node_content` work directly on `OutlineId` and the `String` node id.\n- **Where `node_path` is exercised.** `tests/contracts.rs` (`identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot`) covers stable paths with its own `Application` domain. `tests/storage.rs` and `tests/support/stored_graph.rs` cover filesystem storage with `StoredGraph`. Both use domains other than `Project`, as the commentary says.\n- **Why it needs to exist.** The method is a required trait item. It is a trivial single-segment path with nothing worth testing separately, so leaving it unexecuted in this fixture is acceptable.\n\nThe commentary agrees with the current source, so I found no gap.",
